ed"},{"n":"NEMO (museum)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.374081,"lo":4.91235,"d":491,"ds":"NEMO Science Museum (from Latin: Nemo, lit. 'Nobody') is a science centre in Amsterdam, Netherlands. It is located in the Oosterdokseiland neighbourhood in the Amsterdam-Centrum borough, situated between the Oosterdokseiland and the Kattenburg. The museum has its origins in 1923, and is housed in a building designed by Renzo Piano since 1997.","wpu":"NEMO (museum)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Armsterdam_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Armsterdam_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Basilica of Saint Nicholas, Amsterdam","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.376472,"lo":4.901139,"d":560,"ds":"The Co-cathedral Basilica of Saint Nicholas (Dutch: Co-kathedrale Basiliek van de Heilige Nicolaas) is located in the Old Centre district of Amsterdam, Netherlands, very close to Amsterdam's main railway station. Saint Nicholas is the patron saint of both the church and the city of Amsterdam. The basilica is the city's primary Roman Catholic church.","wpu":"Basilica of Saint Nicholas, Amsterdam","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/AMSTERDAM_HOLLAND_APRIL_2013_%288711705082%29.jpg/960px-AMSTERDAM_HOLLAND_APRIL_2013_%288711705082%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Amsterdam Centre for Architecture","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.372216,"lo":4.912676,"d":689,"ds":"Amsterdam Centre for Architecture (Arcam) is an organisation that was founded in 1986 that \"concentrates its activities in Amsterdam and the surrounding area.\" Arcam focuses on architecture, urban design, and landscape architecture. Arcam is the oldest and largest of more than forty local Dutch architecture centers.","wpu":"Amsterdam Centre for Architecture","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Amsterdam_082.jpg/960px-Amsterdam_082.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ons' Lieve Heer op Solder","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.375076,"lo":4.899363,"d":730,"ds":"Ons' Lieve Heer op Solder (OLHOS; English: Our Lord in the Attic) is a 17th-century canal house, house church, and museum in the city center of Amsterdam, The Netherlands. The Catholic church was built on the top three floors of the canal house during the 1660s.","wpu":"Ons' Lieve Heer op Solder","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Ons%27_Lieve_Heer_op_Solder_2396.jpg/960px-Ons%27_Lieve_Heer_op_Solder_2396.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"He Hua Temple","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.37378,"lo":4.90005,"d":767,"ds":"Fo Guang Shan He Hua Temple (Chinese: 佛光山荷華寺; pinyin: Fó Guāng Shān Hé Huá Sì; lit. 'Buddha's Light Mountain Lotus Flower Temple', or simply He Hua Temple, is a Buddhist temple located at Zeedijk 106–118, Chinatown in Amsterdam. It is the largest Buddhist temple built in the traditional Chinese palace style in Europe.","wpu":"He Hua Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Amsterdam_%2816032323736%29.jpg/960px-Amsterdam_%2816032323736%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Het Scheepvaartmuseum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.371667,"lo":4.914722,"d":804,"ds":"The Maritime Museum is a maritime museum in Amsterdam in the Netherlands. The museum had 419,060 visitors in 2012. It ranked as 12th most visited museum in the Netherlands in 2013.","wpu":"Het Scheepvaartmuseum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Nederlands_Scheepvaartmuseum_2024.jpg/960px-Nederlands_Scheepvaartmuseum_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nieuwmarkt","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.3725,"lo":4.900556,"d":838,"ds":"Nieuwmarkt (Dutch pronunciation: [ˈniuˌmɑr(ə)kt]; English: New Market) is a square in the centre of Amsterdam, Netherlands. The surrounding area is known as the Lastage neighborhood. It is situated in the borough of Amsterdam-Centrum.","wpu":"Nieuwmarkt","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Nieuwmarkt_Amsterdam_during_Koningsdag_2020.jpg/960px-Nieuwmarkt_Amsterdam_during_Koningsdag_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Oudekerksplein","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.374167,"lo":4.897778,"d":872,"ds":"The Oudekerksplein (English: Old Church's Square) is a square in the centre of Amsterdam. It is named after the 14th-century church Oude Kerk which dominates the square. The Oudekerksplein is wedged between the Warmoesstraat street and Oudezijds Voorburgwal canal.","wpu":"Oudekerksplein","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/De_Wallen%2C_Amsterdam%2C_Netherlands_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg/960px-De_Wallen%2C_Amsterdam%2C_Netherlands_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Beit Ha'Chidush","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.370278,"lo":4.905278,"d":895,"ds":"Beit Ha'Chidush (meaning House of Renewal in Hebrew), abbreviated as BHC is a Progressive Jewish congregation, located in Amsterdam, in the North Holland region of The Netherlands. The congregation was founded in 1995 by predominately expatriate Jews with secular and religious backgrounds who wanted to create a welcoming, inspiring and renewed Jewish congregation.","wpu":"Beit Ha'Chidush","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Uilenburg_Synagoge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Hash, Marihuana & Hemp Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.3722,"lo":4.8974,"d":1017,"ds":"The Hash, Marihuana & Hemp Museum is a museum located in De Wallen, Amsterdam, Netherlands. According to the museum, more than two million visitors have visited the exhibition since it opened in 1985. Dedicated to cannabis and its many uses, the museum offers visitors information about the historical and modern uses of cannabis for medicinal, spiritual and cultural purposes.","wpu":"Hash, Marihuana & Hemp Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Marihuanamuseum_Amsterdam.jpg/960px-Marihuanamuseum_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kattenburgervaart","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.371858,"lo":4.920246,"d":1024,"ds":"The Kattenburgervaart is a short canal in Amsterdam that runs through the Oostelijke Eilanden (Eastern Islands). The canal separates the island of Wittenburg, which was built in the 17th century, from the island of Kattenburg. The Kattenburgervaart runs parallel to the Wittenburgervaart (to the east) from the Nieuwe Vaart to the Dijksgracht.","wpu":"Kattenburgervaart","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Ardea_cinerea_-_Amsterdam.jpg/960px-Ardea_cinerea_-_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"W139","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.3735,"lo":4.8956,"d":1038,"ds":"W139 is an artist-run space established in 1979 on the Warmoesstraat, Amsterdam, the Netherlands. The former theatre was squatted in October 1979 by five young artists as \"a movement against the closed world of commercial art and museums\". Currently a group of national and international artists are organising different contemporary art shows by following the W139 artist-run approach.","wpu":"W139","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/W139_1.jpg/960px-W139_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Amsterdam (Dutch: [ˌɑmstərˈdɑm] ; lit. 'Dam in the Amstel') is the capital and largest city of the Netherlands. As of 1 January 2026, it had a population of 941,873 within the city proper, 1,457,018 in the urban area and 2,480,394 in the metropolitan area. Located in the Dutch province of North Holland, Amsterdam is colloquially referred to as the \"Venice of the North\", for its large number of canals, now a UNESCO World Heritage Site.","wpu":"Amsterdam","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Imagen_de_los_canales_conc%C3%A9ntricos_en_%C3%81msterdam.png/960px-Imagen_de_los_canales_conc%C3%A9ntricos_en_%C3%81msterdam.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}